</section>

<!-- Buyer-specific FAQ -->
<section class="buyer">
  <div class="container">
    <SectionHead
      eyebrow="Which questions do we answer?"
      heading="By decision-maker profile"
      description="Factory digitalization isn't one person's decision — it's a team's. Each role asks different questions; our answers speak clearly to each one."
    />
    <div class="buyer-grid" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="100">
      <div class="buyer-card">
        <span class="role-tag">Production &amp; Maintenance</span>
        <h3>How does it affect operations?</h3>
        <p class="q">"Is this another system on the floor? Will operators use it? Will it interfere with automation?"</p>
        <div class="ans">Predictivo doesn't touch your existing PLC/SCADA; it reads data via OPC UA or Modbus. There's no extra logging workload for operators — in fact, start- and end-of-shift reports become automatic. Pilots start with a single machine or a single line.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="buyer-card">
        <span class="role-tag">IT &amp; OT</span>
        <h3>Security &amp; integration architecture?</h3>
        <p class="q">"Can we get data without touching the OT network? Is there RBAC, audit, on-prem support?"</p>
        <div class="ans">The edge gateway can connect to the OT network in read-only mode; data flows one-way through a DMZ. The whole system runs on token-based RBAC, audit logging, and TLS. On-premise, private cloud, or hybrid deployment is supported.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="buyer-card">
        <span class="role-tag">General Manager / CFO</span>
        <h3>What's the return on investment?</h3>
        <p class="q">"If we apply it to one line, how much difference will we see? How do we scale after the pilot?"</p>
        <div class="ans">Pilots typically start with one line or one group of machines; OEE, unplanned downtime, and energy consumption are measured before and after. Typical payback is 12-18 months; after that it scales across the whole facility.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

